---
description: Require a squash-commit changelog line, or a version bump that cuts a release
alwaysApply: true
---

# Changelog entries

Every pull request takes **one** of two shapes.

## Entry

Add **one** line to `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]`.

The line is exactly the squash-merge subject and the PR number. The squash subject is the PR title (Conventional Commits). Do not invent a different summary.

```markdown
- <pr title> (#<pr number>)
```

```
# ❌ BAD
- Improved linting
- feat(proto): add lot spec
  (missing PR number; mixed into the feature commit)

# ✅ GOOD
- feat(proto): add lot spec (#12)
  (own commit that only changes CHANGELOG.md)
```

The changelog line is **always** its own commit:

- That commit touches **only** `CHANGELOG.md`
- Do not mix the line with schema, CI, docs, or other edits
- Open the PR first, then add this commit once the number is known
- If the PR title changes, update the line to match

Do not commit the changelog line until the PR exists. Feature commits land first; the changelog commit is last.

## Release

Bump the version in **both** `pubspec.yaml` and `pyproject.toml` to the same new value, and move every `## [Unreleased]` bullet under a new heading, leaving Unreleased empty:

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

## [0.2.0] - 2026-09-07

- feat(proto): add lot spec (#12)
```

The heading must be `## [<version>] - YYYY-MM-DD` and the bullets must be the former Unreleased entries, in order.

A release PR does not add a squash-subject line under Unreleased. Publishing a version tag requires Unreleased to be empty.
